== Effects ==
* When Isaac's normal tears disappear (either from hitting the ground or hitting something else), they spawn 4 smaller tears.
** Each smaller tear deals half of Isaac's normal [[damage]].
** Split tears are scaled down by 0.6x from the main ones, ignoring damage-based size reduction.
* {{Dlc|nr}} Tear size multiplier: 1.2x.
* {{Dlc|r}} +0.1 tear size.
* {{dlc|nr}} {{tear delay down|1}}
* {{dlc|r}} +0.5 [[fire rate]].
* {{dlc|nr}} -10 [[range]].
* {{dlc|r}} 0.8x [[range]] multiplier.

== Notes ==
* Split tears will inherit the main tear's [[status effect]], if any.
* If Isaac has less than {{dlc|nr}}10 range/{{dlc|r}}10 [[tear height]], the split tears appear but cannot cause damage before hitting the floor.
** {{dlc|nr}} {{c|Cain}}, {{c|Lazarus}}, and {{c|Samson}} have lower starting range and are particularly susceptible.
** [[Tear falling speed]] ups can't mitigate this downside.

== Synergies ==
* {{i|Angelic Prism}}: All tears split by the prism will burst into split tears.
* {{i|Bob's Rotten Head}}: Bob's Rotten Head splits into four smaller heads on detonation.
* {{i|Compound Fracture}}: When bone tears split into bone shards after hitting an obstacle or enemy, the bone shards will split into 4 smaller bone shards after hitting the ground.
* {{i|Explosivo}}: The explosion results in split Explosivo shots being generated. {{dlc|nr}} If the target survives, they're likely to immediately stick again. {{dlc|r}} The split tears explode when they hit an enemy or the ground.
* {{i|Haemolacria}}: Main tears can split as they burst upon hitting the floor, an obstacle, or an enemy. The split tears can burst, but burst tears from main tears do not split.
** Cricket's Body's x0.8 range multiplier does not stack with Haemolacria's own x0.8 range multiplier.
* {{i|Ipecac}}: Main tear splits into four explosive splash tears. The split tears can still damage Isaac. Having {{i|Host Hat}} or {{i|Pyromaniac}} is strongly recommended.
** {{dlc|r}} Cricket's Body's x0.8 range multiplier does not stack with Ipecac's own x0.8 range multiplier.
* {{i|Lachryphagy}}: Fed tears split into 12 tears.
* {{i|Lead Pencil}}/{{i|Monstro's Lung}}: All tears fired will splash after landing. Increased damage potential only noticed when firing into groups, due to the random pattern of each tear when it splashes.
* {{i|The Parasite}}: Eight split tears instead of four.
* {{i|Tiny Planet}}: The split tears orbit Isaac instead of spreading.
* {{i|Tough Love}}: Teeth tears will split into 4 smaller teeth.
* {{i|Tractor Beam}}: Main tears and split tears will travel along the beam.

== Interactions ==
* {{dlc|nr}} {{i|Brimstone}}: Overrides Cricket's Body.
** {{dlc|r}} Small red brimstone tears will fire out upon the beam hitting a wall or enemy.
** {{dlc|r}} '''Brimstone''' + {{i|Soy Milk}}: Brimstone tears always fire out at the end of the beam.
* {{i|Dead Onion}}: Significantly decreases effective range, potentially preventing the split tears from causing damage.
* {{i|Diplopia}}: No effect.
* {{i|Dr. Fetus|na}}: Reduces range, bombs do not split.
** {{dlc|anr}} Reduces range, the bombs fired by Dr. Fetus will split into smaller bombs, much like {{i|Scatter Bombs|n}}.
** {{dlc|r}} Increases range, the bombs fired by Dr. Fetus will split into smaller bombs, much like {{i|Scatter Bombs|n}}.
* {{i|Epic Fetus}}: Only tear stat change applies.
* {{i|Euthanasia}}: Needle tears will split into 4 small needle tears upon hitting the ground or an enemy. Split tears produced have a chance to deal triple damage but will not cause tear bursts.
* {{i|Fire Mind}}: Main tear splits into four explosive splash tears. Having {{i|Host Hat}} or {{i|Pyromaniac}} is strongly recommended.
* {{i|Flat Stone}}: Tears will usually only bounce twice, unless Isaac has high range, and spawn burst tears when they bounce.
* {{T|Hook Worm}}: Split tears gain a significant range increase, allowing them to potentially hit farther targets
* {{i|Kidney Stone}}: Drastically decreases range, potentially preventing the split tears from causing damage. The stone will not split.
* {{i|The Ludovico Technique}}: Overrides Cricket's Body except for stat effects which apply.
* {{i|Mom's Knife}}: Range of the knife is significantly decreased.
* {{i|Number One}}: Tears disappear '''very''' quickly after being fired, and split tears barely travel at all.
** {{dlc|r}} '''Not recommended.''' Unlike other similar items, Cricket's Body's x0.8 range multiplier does stack with Number One's own x0.8 range multiplier, thus drastically reducing range.
* [[Piercing]] tears: Tears will only split after landing on the ground.
* [[Spectral]] tears: Tears will only split after landing on the ground.
* {{dlc|nr}}{{i|Technology}}/{{i|Tech X|dlc=anr}}: Overrides Cricket's Body. Stat effects still apply.
** {{dlc|r}} Cricket's Body tear splitting effect applies when lasers hit something.

